result, _compute_label_hmac's Path(__file__).parents[1] still resolves to .claude/hooks/_lib, and the label store and label-chain key do not change.\n13\t2. Fail direction.\n14\t- If a fragment file is missing (partial install), the facade raises before any decision. _python-hook.sh then passes the hook's own exit code through, so the session continues: fail-open on an infrastructure fault, the same class as the unguarded _lib imports the monolith already had.\n15\t- decisions_cli.main keeps the existing catch-all that allows on infrastructure errors. Its two new blocks are both wrapped in try/except, so neither can change the verdict: the bash_indirect_telemetry call (decisions_cli.py:168-174) and the reason_code veto_triggered emit (:195-202).\n16\t- The fact-gate paths are byte-identical to before: infrastructure errors leave the incoming block unchanged, and a command that cannot be normalized is never released.\n17\t3. Writes.\n18\t- Fragment and facade write targets are unchanged.\n19\t- The new telemetry marker (bash_indirect_telemetry.py:52-58) is created with O_CREAT|O_EXCL, mode 0600, under the audit family directory.\n20\t4. Python and stdlib.\n21\t- Every import in these files is stdlib or _lib.\n22\t- I found no 3.10+ syntax. FunctionType(code, globals, name, defaults, closure) works on 3.9.\n23\t5. Declared conditions in this payload's reach.\n24\t- Condition 5: the rows .claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_log_parts/**/* and _bash_safety_parts/**/* are at check_arbitration_kernel.py:313-314. _match_segments lets ** match zero segments, so files directly inside the package are kernel.\n25\t- Condition 6: the switches are read from the trusted_env snapshot (posture_scan.py:573-574, decisions_cli.py:170-172).\n26\t- Condition 7 and the CHANGELOG \"Changed — hooks and scripts split\" section: install.sh:1524-1541 copies every top-level _lib entry, so the new packages ship. check_bash_safety.py is 42 lines, as claimed.\n27\t- I found nothing in these files that makes