cade's.\n39\tP2-4. .claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts/decisions_cli.py:195-202, together with fact_canonical.py:147 and fact_state.py:23/38/54. The new veto_triggered emit, keyed on reason_code, reads only the final decision. When the fact gate in ENFORCE mode, or the ADR-175 citation pilot, replaces a bash_indirect_* block, the new Decision is built without reason_code. Scenario: on those paths no veto_triggered event with the indirect reason code is written; only the fact-gate or citation events are. This affects audit records only; the block decision is unchanged. Minimal fix: pass reason_code=decision.reason_code into the replacement Decision constructors.\n40\t\n41\tVERDICT: GO The fragments in this payload match the pre-split code wherever I compared them, keep the fail-open and fail-closed directions, stay stdlib-only and Python 3.9-compatible, are covered by the condition-5 kernel rows, and make no declared condition false; the only findings are four P2 follow-ups.\n42\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4ead31fb-64db-4d2c-9f7e-f45956681e3d","uuid":"1931f4ce-acb9-495e-8042-155b5c1887c3","timestamp":"2026-11-16T17:56:29.430Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/kit-repass-tree.n5R3O9/tree/.claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/claude-rc1-04.verdict.txt","content":"PAYLOAD 4/32. Files: the new fragments under .claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_log_parts (paths_skills.py, rotation_storage.py), .claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_query/* (9 files) and .claude/hooks/_lib/_bash_safety_parts (__init__.py, decisions_cli.py, fact_canonical.py, fact_state.py). I read them together with the facades that load them (audit_log.py:305-329, check_bash_safety.py:1-42, .claude/scripts/audit-query.py:174-385). I compared them with the pre-split staged copies in .claude/plans/PLAN-182/staged-w1 and with the PLAN-194 auditrace patch.\n\nFINDINGS\nP0: none.\nP1: none.\n\nWHAT I CHECKED\n1. Moved code. These checks matter for condition 7.\n- I compared these functions with the pre-split copies, and their text matches: audit_paths, rotate_threshold, write_breadcrumb, _is_safe_audit_path, _fallback_security_breadcrumb, _apply_destructive_citation_gate, _apply_fact_gate and the _E3_* tables.\n- append_entry plus _emit_rotation_marker_under_lock match the PLAN-194 cure of condition 67, which this release carries: one FileLock with timeout 2.5 covers key, predecessor read, HMAC, append and sidecar. That cure stays in place.\n- The audit_log and check_bash_safety facades run each fragment with exec in the facade's own globals. So __file__ is still the facade's (normalization.py:190 _HOOKS_DIR resolves to .claude/hooks). Monkeypatch points and global lookups behave as before. No top-level statement uses a name from a later fragment. The cross-fragment constants (_DESTRUCTIVE_CITE_VAR, _ENV_ASSIGNMENT_RE, _CITE_*) are defined by earlier fragments. The only duplicate top-level assignment, _PRIVILEGE_PREFIXES at normalization.py:91/103, is also in the monolith.\n- audit-query.py binds every extracted function to its own globals with FunctionType. It also restores _LABEL_STORE_PATH at audit-query.py:203. As a result, _compute_label_hmac's Path(__file__).parents[1] still resolves to .claude/hooks/_lib, and the label store and label-chain key do not change.\n2. Fail direction.\n- If a fragment file is missing (partial install), the facade raises before any decision. _python-hook.sh then passes the hook's own exit code through, so the session continues: fail-open on an infrastructure fault, the same class as the unguarded _lib imports the monolith already had.\n- decisions_cli.main keeps the existing catch-all that allows on infrastructure errors. Its two new blocks are both wrapped in try/except, so neither can change the verdict: the bash_indirect_telemetry call (decisions_cli.py:168-174) and the reason_code veto_triggered emit (:195-202).\n- The fact-gate paths are byte-identical to before: