{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xfdsu2zxCt6vb7AZX4B2QY","type":"tool_result","content":".claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/claude-rc1-03.verdict.txt:1:SCOPE: payload 3/32. It has 12 new files under .claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_emit_parts/ (orchestration, pair_rail, planning, rate_limits, replay, resource_events, routing, security, streaming, tokens_boot, workflow, writer) and 3 under .claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_log_parts/ (__init__, adapters_runtime, entries_usage). They are PLAN-197 moves behind the _lib/audit_emit.py and audit_log.py facades.\n.claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/claude-rc1-03.verdict.txt:9:   audit_log.py:311-327 runs the four part sources with exec in its own globals, in the order paths_skills, entries_usage, rotation_storage, adapters_runtime. The trailing `if __name__ == \"__main__\": sys.exit(main())` in adapters_runtime.py runs only after all four are installed.\n.claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/claude-rc1-03.verdict.txt:23:   - The codex, grok and claude paths in adapters_runtime.py return 0 on every path. Their logic matches the staged copy .claude/plans/PLAN-182/staged-w1/tree/.claude/hooks/audit_log.py:1360-1615.\n.claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/claude-rc1-03.verdict.txt:58:- Minimal fix: wrap _install_parts in try/except, write a breadcrumb, and exit 0 when run as __main__.\n.claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/claude-rc1-03.verdict.txt:73:- Related hygiene: _audit_log_parts/entries_usage.py and adapters_runtime.py cannot be imported as standalone modules (re, os and sys are unbound), even though the directory is a package. In production they are only run by the facade.\n.claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/claude-rc1-21.verdict.txt:25:  compile() also inherits the facade's `annotations` future flag. decisions_cli.py:252 keeps the `if __name__ == \"__main__\"` guard, and it runs last, after all eight fragments are loaded. No __all__ existed before or after.\n.claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/claude-rc1-21.verdict.txt:45:5. P2 (load-order invariant is untested), check_bash_safety.py:20-23. The entry point runs main() from inside the exec loop, through decisions_cli's __main__ guard. Any fragment appended after \"decisions_cli\" would load only after main() has already run and exited. Fix: drop the guard from decisions_cli, put `if __name__ == \"__main__\": sys.exit(main())` in the facade after _install_parts(), or assert that _PARTS[-1] == \"decisions_cli\".\n.claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/claude-rc1-05.verdict.txt:5:- Namespace semantics: the monolith already used `from __future__ import annotations` (staged copy line 60) and compile() inherits it, so annotation semantics are unchanged. __file__ is the facade path, so _HOOKS_DIR = .claude/hooks as before. The `if __name__ == \"__main__\"` guard in decisions_cli.py:252 fires only as a script. Test patch points on the facade reach every part because the namespace is shared.\n.claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/claude-rc1-22.verdict.txt:5:- Condition 7: true. check_canonical_edit.py keeps its path, its __main__ dispatch and the --is-canonical oracle (:643-651). All logic now lives in _lib/canonical_edit/{paths,sentinels,signature_rail,session_roots,utility,decisions,entry,guards}.py, so a hand-applied patch has to be applied again in the module.\n.claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/claude-rc1-20.verdict.txt:13:2. Fail direction: unchanged. Under __main__ (the shim execs the script, _python-hook.sh:416), a part load failure prints {} and exits 0 (check_agent_spawn.py:126-135), which is byte-identical to the adapter allow (_lib/adapters/claude.py:141-157). Entrypoint.py:12-16 and :63-69 keep the runtime fail-open. The Bash-side guard still covers the moved code through _CANONICAL_GUARDS \".claude/hooks/_lib/**/*.py\" (canonical_edit/guards.py:34, consumed by _bash_safety_parts/posture_tables.py:53/71).\n.claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/claude-rc1-20.verdict.txt:15:[Omitted long matching line]\n.claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/claude-rc1-20.verdict.txt:22:- check_agent_spawn.py:640-647: a bind() failure is swallowed into _SPAWN_COMPONENT_IMPORT_ERROR, which only main() consults. In-process importers (spawn_agent.py:92, self_test.py:262) would then get a NameError on every decide() call instead of a clear import error. This is practically unreachable, because install() already imported _lib.agent_spawn, whose __init__ imports both components and would raise first. Minimal fix: re-raise when __name__ != \"__main__\", mirroring _load_spawn_part.\n.claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/claude-rc1-12.verdict.txt:13:- Fail direction is preserved: a component load failure under __main__ prints {} (allow) and exits 0, and main() allows when _SPAWN_COMPONENT_IMPORT_ERROR is set. That is fail-open on an infrastructure fault. The fail-closed input checks inside decide() are unchanged.\n.claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/claude-rc1-19.verdict.txt:16:- The audit_log.py parts are identical to the base text, including the _ADR_052_ROLE_TO_MODEL table, so no model value changes. The `if __name__ == \"__main__\"` block sits in the last part, so main() runs only after every declaration is installed. __doc__ is restored.\n.claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/claude-rc1-19.verdict.txt:59:- Fix: wrap _install_parts() in try/except, write a stderr breadcrumb, and exit 0 when run as __main__."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4ead31fb-64db-4d2c-9f7e-f45956681e3d","uuid":"4c9ecbb6-47d9-4bb4-8923-a60012b18cd2","timestamp":"2026-11-16T18:00:58.851Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":".claude/plans/PLAN-198/repass-rc1/claude-rc1-03.verdict.txt:1:SCOPE: payload 3/32. It has 12 new files under .claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_emit_parts/ (orchestration, pair_rail, planning, rate_limits, replay, resource_events, routing, security, streaming, tokens_boot, workflow, writer) and 3 under .claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_log_parts/ (__init__, adapters_runtime, entries_usage). They are PLAN-