s unchanged, the code is standard-library only and Python 3.9-compatible, the two audit part packages are kernel-listed, and no declared condition is false and no P0 or new P1 was found.\",\"report\":\"SCOPE: payload 4/34 (GA). Files: _lib/_audit_emit_parts/{workflow,writer}.py; _lib/_audit_log_parts/{__init__,adapters_runtime,entries_usage,paths_skills,rotation_storage}.py; _lib/_audit_query/{__init__,critical,domain,labeling,parsing}.py. I read them together with the facades that load them: _lib/audit_emit.py:413-452 with _audit_emit_parts/__init__.py:20-48 (install binder); audit_log.py:309-329 (exec loader); .claude/scripts/audit-query.py:174-228 (FunctionType rebinding). I compared the moved text with the base deletions in the rc evidence (diff-rc1-14.patch for audit_emit, diff-rc1-19.patch for audit_log, diff-rc1-24.patch for audit-query). Per the GA-only condition, the code is byte-identical to the rc.\\n\\nP0: none.\\n\\nNEW FINDINGS (annex): none at P1.\\n\\nDECLARED CONDITIONS THIS PAYLOAD TOUCHES (all TRUE against the code)\\n- Condition 3 / rc condition 67 (carried cure): append_entry (rotation_storage.py) still holds ONE FileLock (timeout 2.5) around rotation, marker, key, predecessor read, HMAC, append and last-hmac sidecar. Its text is identical to the base at diff-rc1-19.patch:3271-3434, including _emit_rotation_marker_under_lock and the chain_reset_marker_missing branch.\\n- Condition 5: both rows are present at check_arbitration_kernel.py:312-313: '.claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_emit_parts/**/*' and '.claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_log_parts/**/*'. _audit_query is not on the list, and neither is its entry point .claude/scripts/audit-query.py, so moving the logic takes nothing out of kernel protection.\\n- Condition 7: audit_log.py, _lib/audit_emit.py and .claude/scripts/audit-query.py keep their paths, and the logic now lives in the _lib packages. install.sh:1524-1541 copies every top-level _lib entry; _framework_path_excluded (_framework_manifest_set.sh:95-107) excludes none of the new packages.\\n- Conditions 13 and 14: nothing in this payload bears on scope or withheld counts.\\n\\nWHAT I CHECKED\\n1. Moved code and name lookup:\\n- audit_emit: install() deep-copies each part's __all__ into the facade, then rebinds every function to the facade globals. So global _FALLBACK_NOTIFIED (writer.py) mutates facade state, and patch points on _lib.audit_emit reach _write_event, _preview, _breadcrumb and the rest.\\n- Every free name in writer.py and workflow.py resolves in the facade: getpass, json, os, sys, datetime, timezone, Path, FileLock, FileLockTimeout, _redact, _runtime_paths, _audit_hmac, _spool_writer, _KNOWN_ACTIONS, EVENT_SCHEMA_V2, and _AUDIT_PRODUCER_PATH_POLLUTION_REASON_CODES (operations.py:463).\\n- _write_event, _emit_chain_reset_marker_under_lock, _preview and the emitters I spot-checked match the base text (diff-rc1-14.patch:2884-3130, :3311, :3360, :3507, :3716). _ensure_canonical_lib_modules (audit_hmac.py:760) still sees _lib.audit_emit.__file__ in _lib, so the producer-path-pollution chokepoints are unaffected.\\n- audit_log: the fragments run with exec in the facade dictionary, in the order paths_skills, entries_usage, rotation_storage, adapters_runtime. __file__ stays the hook path. Every name they use (stat, getpass, Tuple, _rp_state_dir, the _SKILL_* regexes, _ARCHETYPE_*) is defined in the facade before the exec. The _ADR_052_ROLE_TO_MODEL table is unchanged, so no model value changes.\\n- audit-query: domain, rendering, labeling, critical and parsing are copied by __all__, and the __all__ lists are complete for each module's top-level names. queries, reporting and reporting_health have no module-level constants, so rebinding their functions alone is enough.\\n- _LABEL_STORE_PATH is restored at audit-query.py:203, and _compute_label_hmac's Path(__file__).parents[1] resolves to .claude/hooks/_lib. The label store and the label-chain key are therefore unchanged; the base text is at diff-rc1-24.patch:1966-2000. The MCP loader (mcp-server/handlers/audit_query.py:127-135) loads the facade by path, so the same binding applies. label stays excluded from the MCP allowlist.\\n2. Fail direction: unchanged.\\n- Audit writers stay fail-open everywhere.\\n- A missing _audit_log_parts file raises at import; the hook exits 1, which does not block a PostToolUse event (_python-hook.sh derives exit 2 only from an emitted deny).\\n- A missing _audit_query module makes the MCP handler fail open, with an import_failed warning.\\n3. Writes: no target moved. That covers the audit log, the lock and errors files (family-follows-log), the /tmp fallback and the label store.\\n4. Python and stdlib: standard library plus _lib only, and no 3.10+ syntax. Annotations such as \\\"_contract.NormalizedEvent | _payload.HookPayload\\\" and List[...] are strings under from __future__ import annotations.\\n5. Honesty: critical.py's \\\"38 critical-security actions\\\" is correct (12+3+7+3+2+1+10). The label docstrings (\\\"Append-only via HMAC chain to .claude/scripts/audit-log-labels.jsonl\\\") hold through the facade.\\n\\nCARRIED, ALREADY DECLARED (re-confirmed, not new)\\n- writer.py:603-604/687/761: when mkdir or the FileLock open raises OSError before 'line' exists, the code raises UnboundLocalError and the event is lost with no /tmp fallback. This is the codex-p03 P1 in the signed lane notes. The base had the same text (diff-rc1-14.patch:3106-3110).\\n\\nP2 FOLLOW-UPS (new)\\nP2-1. audit_log.py:311-327 with _audit_log_parts/adapters_runtime.py:258-259.\\n- Defect: when the hook runs as a script, main() is called from inside the exec loop, through the 'if __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\": sys.exit(main())' guard at the end of the last fragment. The loop and the __doc__ restore at :328 never finish.\\n- Scenario: a maintainer appends a fifth part after \\\"adapters_runtime\\\" in _PARTS. When the hook runs, main() executes and exits before that part is loaded, so every name defined there is missing at runtime; imports in tests would still see it. This is the same class as the rc P2 for check_bash_safety (claude-rc1-21 P2-5), which the rc did not raise for audit_log.\\n- Minimal fix: remove the guard from the fragment and put 'if __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\": sys.exit(main())' in audit_log.py after _install_parts(), or assert _PARTS[-1] == \\\"adapters_runtime\\\".\\nP2-2. _audit_query/domain.py:56-101 (_resolve_window_bounds), reached through mcp-server/handlers/audit_query.py:86 and :172.\\n- Defect: an invalid 'window' value calls sys.exit(1). SystemExit is a BaseException, so it passes through the handler's 'except Exception' (handlers/audit_query.py:321), dispatch.py:755 and stdio_transport.run.\\n- Scenario: an authenticated MCP client sends audit_query.by_domain with params {\\\"window\\\": \\\"x\\\"}. The read-only stdio MCP server process exits. This behaviour predates this release, but the moved helper keeps it.\\n- Minimal fix: raise ValueError in the helper and turn it into exit 1 in audit-query main(), or catch SystemExit in the MCP handler.\\nP2-3. _audit_log_parts/rotation_storage.py:154-171 (_fallback_security_breadcrumb).\\n- Defect: it appends to the predictable /tmp/ceo-audit-fallback-<user>.log with open(\\\"a\\\"), which follows symlinks. It also ignores CEO_AUDIT_LOG_FALLBACK_PATH, although its docstring says it \\\"Mirrors _lib.audit_emit._fallback_log_path\\\". This predates the release and is the same class as claude-rc1-03 P2-2 (writer.py).\\n- Minimal fix: os.open with O_WRONLY|O_APPEND|O_CREAT|O_NOFOLLOW and mode 0o600, and honour the override.\\n\\nP2 FOLLOW-UPS (carried from the rc re-pass, re-confirmed in this payload's files)\\n- workflow.py: List annotations on the bound emitters make typing.get_type_hints raise NameError, because the facade imports only Any, Dict and Optional (claude-rc1-03 P2-5).\\n- labeling.py:19/51: correct only when rebound by the facade. Used standalone, the store path points inside _lib, and audit_hmac fails to import, so the fixed fallback key is used. No such caller exists today (claude-rc1-04 P2-3).\\n- domain.py:241-251: a malformed sunset_reopen_* value becomes False, against the documented True default (codex-rc1-04 P2).\\n- writer.py:42-51/76/87: the /tmp fallback follows symlinks (claude-rc1-03 P2-2).\\n- audit_log.py:317-327: a missing part file makes the hook exit 1 with a traceback instead of writing a breadcrumb and exiting 0 (claude-rc1-03 P2-3).\"}","structured_output":{"decision":"GO","sentence":"Payload 4/34 moves the audit_emit writer and workflow emitters, the audit_log parts and the audit-query parts without changing behaviour: the text matches the base, the facades rebind every name, write locations stay put, the fail direction is unchanged, the code is standard-library only and Python 3.9-compatible, the two audit part packages are kernel-listed, and no declared condition is false and no P0 or new P1 was found.","report":"SCOPE: payload 4/34 (GA). Files: _lib/_audit_emit_parts/{workflow,writer}.py; _lib/_audit_log_parts/{__init__,adapters_runtime,entries_usage,paths_skills,rotation_storage}.py; _lib/_audit_query/{__init__,critical,domain,labeling,parsing}.py. I read them together with the facades that load them: _lib/audit_emit.py:413-452 with _audit_emit_parts/__init__.py:20-48 (install binder); audit_log.py:309-329 (exec loader); .claude/scripts/audit-query.py:174-228 (FunctionType rebinding). I compared the moved text with the base deletions in the rc evidence (diff-rc1-14.patch for audit_emit, diff-rc1-19.patch for audit_log, diff-rc1-24.patch for audit-query). Per the GA-only condition, the code is byte-identical to the rc.\n\nP0: none.\n\nNEW FINDINGS (annex): none at P1.\n\nDECLARED CONDITIONS THIS PAYLOAD TOUCHES (all TRUE against the code)\n- Condition 3 / rc condition 67 (carried cure): append_entry (rotation_storage.py) still holds ONE FileLock (timeout 2.5) around rotation, marker, key, predecessor read, HMAC, append and last-hmac sidecar. Its text is identical to the base at diff-rc1-19.patch:3271-3434, including _emit_rotation_marker_under_lock and the chain_reset_marker_missing branch.\n- Condition 5: both rows are present at check_arbitration_kernel.py:312-313: '.claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_emit_parts/**/*' and '.claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_log_parts/**/*'. _audit_query is not on the list, and neither is its entry point .claude/scripts/audit-query.py, so moving the logic takes nothing out of kernel protection.\n- Condition 7: audit_log.py, _lib/audit_emit.py and .claude/scripts/audit-query.py keep their paths, and the logic now lives in the _lib packages. install.sh:1524-1541 copies every top-level _lib entry; _framework_path_excluded (_framework_manifest_set.sh:95-107) excludes none of the new packages.\n- Conditions 13 and 14: nothing in this payload bears on scope or withheld counts.\n\nWHAT I CHECKED\n1. Moved code and name lookup:\n- audit_emit: install() deep-copies each part's __all__ into the facade, then rebinds every function to the facade globals. So global _FALLBACK_NOTIFIED (writer.py) mutates facade state, and patch points on _lib.audit_emit reach _write_event, _preview, _breadcrumb and the rest.\n- Every free name in writer.py and workflow.py resolves in the facade: getpass, json, os, sys, datetime, timezone, Path, FileLock, FileLockTimeout, _redact, _runtime_paths, _audit_hmac, _spool_writer, _KNOWN_ACTIONS, EVENT_SCHEMA_V2, and _AUDIT_PRODUCER_PATH_POLLUTION_REASON_CODES (operations.py:463).\n- _write_event, _emit_chain_reset_marker_under_lock, _preview and the emitters I spot-checked match the base text (diff-rc1-14.patch:2884-3130, :3311, :3360, :3507, :3716). _ensure_canonical_lib_modules (audit_hmac.py:760) still sees _lib.audit_emit.__file__ in _lib, so the producer-path-pollution chokepoints are unaffected.\n- audit_log: the fragments run with exec in the facade dictionary, in the order paths_skills, entries_usage, rotation_storage, adapters_runtime. __file__ stays the hook path. Every name they use (stat, getpass, Tuple, _rp_state_dir, the _SKILL_* regexes, _ARCHETYPE_*) is defined in the facade before the exec. The _ADR_052_ROLE_TO_MODEL table is unchanged, so no model value changes.\n- audit-query: domain, rendering, labeling, critical and parsing are copied by __all__, and the __all__ lists are complete for each module's top-level names. queries, reporting and reporting_health have no module-level constants, so rebinding their functions alone is enough.\n- _LABEL_STORE_PATH is restored at audit-query.py:203, and _compute_label_hmac's Path(__file__).parents[1] resolves to .claude/hooks/_lib. The label store and the label-chain key are therefore unchanged; the base text is at diff-rc1-24.patch:1966-2000. The MCP loader (mcp-server/handlers/audit_query.py:127-135) loads the facade by path, so the same binding applies. label stays excluded from the MCP allowlist.\n2. Fail direction: unchanged.\n- Audit writers stay fail-open everywhere.\n- A missing _audit_log_parts file raises at import; the hook exits 1, which does not block a PostToolUse event (_python-hook.sh derives exit 2 only from an emitted deny).\n- A missing _audit_query module makes the MCP handler fail open, with an import_failed warning.\n3. Writes: no target moved. That covers the audit log, the lock and errors files (family-follows-log), the /tmp fallback and the label store.\n4. Python and stdlib: standard library plus _lib only, and no 3.10+ syntax. Annotations such as \"_contract.NormalizedEvent | _payload.HookPayload\" and List[...] are strings under from __future__ import annotations.\n5. Honesty: critical.py's \"38 critical-security actions\" is correct (12+3+7+3+2+1+10). The label docstrings (\"Append-only via HMAC chain to .claude/scripts/audit-log-labels.jsonl\") hold through the facade.\n\nCARRIED, ALREADY DECLARED (re-confirmed, not new)\n- writer.py:603-604/687/761: when mkdir or the FileLock open raises OSError before 'line' exists, the code raises UnboundLocalError and the event is lost with no /tmp fallback. This is the codex-p03 P1 in the signed lane notes. The base had the same text (diff-rc1-14.patch:3106-3110).\n\nP2 FOLLOW-UPS (new)\nP2-1. audit_log.py:311-327 with _audit_log_parts/adapters_runtime.py:258-259.\n- Defect: when the hook runs as a script, main() is called from inside the exec loop, through the 'if __name__ == \"__main__\": sys.exit(main())' guard at the end of the last fragment. The loop and the __doc__ restore at :328 never finish.\n- Scenario: a maintainer appends a fifth part after \"adapters_runtime\" in _PARTS. When the hook runs, main() executes and exits before that part is loaded, so every name defined there is missing at runtime; imports in tests would still see it. This is the same class as the rc P2 for check_bash_safety (claude-rc1-21 P2-5), which the rc did not raise for audit_log.\n- Minimal fix: remove the guard from the fragment and put 'if __name__ == \"__main__\": sys.exit(main())' in audit_log.py after _install_parts(), or assert _PARTS[-1] == \"adapters_runtime\".\nP2-2. _audit_query/domain.py:56-101 (_resolve_window_bounds), reached through mcp-server/handlers/audit_query.py:86 and :172.\n- Defect: an invalid 'window' value calls sys.exit(1). SystemExit is a BaseException, so it passes through the handler's 'except Exception' (handlers/audit_query.py:321), dispatch.py:755 and stdio_transport.run.\n- Scenario: an authenticated MCP client sends audit_query.by_domain with params {\"window\": \"x\"}. The read-only stdio MCP server process exits. This behaviour predates this release, but the moved helper keeps it.\n- Minimal fix: raise ValueError in the helper and turn it into exit 1 in audit-query main(), or catch SystemExit in the MCP handler.\nP2-3. _audit_log_parts/rotation_storage.py:154-171 (_fallback_security_breadcrumb).\n- Defect: it appends to the predictable /tmp/ceo-audit-fallback-<user>.log with open(\"a\"), which follows symlinks. It also ignores CEO_AUDIT_LOG_FALLBACK_PATH, although its docstring says it \"Mirrors _lib.audit_emit._fallback_log_path\". This predates the release and is the same class as claude-rc1-03 P2-2 (writer.py).\n- Minimal fix: os.open with O_WRONLY|O_APPEND|O_CREAT|O_NOFOLLOW and mode 0o600, and honour the override.\n\nP2 FOLLOW-UPS (carried from the rc re-pass, re-confirmed in this payload's files)\n- workflow.py: List annotations on the bound emitters make typing.get_type_hints raise NameError, because the facade imports only Any, Dict and Optional (claude-rc1-03 P2-5).\n- labeling.py:19/51: correct only when rebound by the facade. Used standalone, the store path points inside _lib, and audit_hmac fails to import, so the fixed fallback key is used. No such caller exists today (claude-rc1-04 P2-3).\n- domain.py:241-251: a malformed sunset_reopen_* value becomes False, against the documented True default (codex-rc1-04 P2).\n- writer.py:42-51/76/87: the /tmp fallback follows symlinks (claude-rc1-03 P2-2).\n- audit_log.py:317-327: a missing part file makes the hook exit 1 with a traceback instead of writing a breadcrumb and exiting 0 (claude-rc1-03 P2-3)."},"ttft_ms":19789,"type":"result","duration_ms":444006,"uuid":"ad423f44-0d27-4058-b93b-b3683b85737f","ttft_stream_ms":7237,"time_to_request_ms":187,"first_content_frame_ms":7238,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":94,"outputTokens":35087,"cacheReadInputTokens":7623716,"cacheCreationInputTokens":206407,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":3.8781152000000003,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":20133,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":206407,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-20T15:54:23.997Z"}
